@startuml API-Sync-Sequence
!theme plain

title External API Synchronization - Sequence Diagram

actor User
participant "Frontend\n(Svelte)" as FE
participant "API Layer" as API
participant "Tauri Backend\n(Rust)" as TB
participant "Auth Service" as AS
participant "API Clients" as AC
database "SQLite" as DB
participant "Steam API" as STEAM
participant "HLTV" as HLTV
participant "Faceit API" as FACEIT

== Steam Authentication ==

User -> FE: Click "Connect Steam"
activate FE

FE -> API: initSteamAuth()
activate API
API -> TB: invoke("init_steam_auth")
activate TB

TB -> AS: start_oauth_flow()
activate AS
AS -> AS: Generate state token
AS -> AS: Build OAuth URL
AS --> TB: OAuth URL
deactivate AS

TB -> TB: Open system browser\nwith OAuth URL
TB --> API: {status: "awaiting_callback"}
deactivate TB
API --> FE: Show "Waiting for Steam..."
deactivate API

note over STEAM: User logs in to Steam\nand authorizes app

STEAM -> TB: OAuth callback with code
activate TB
TB -> AS: handle_callback(code)
activate AS
AS -> AC: exchange_code(code)
activate AC
AC -> STEAM: POST /token
STEAM --> AC: access_token, refresh_token
AC --> AS: Tokens
deactivate AC

AS -> DB: Store encrypted tokens
AS --> TB: AuthSuccess(steam_id)
deactivate AS

TB --> FE: Event: auth_complete
deactivate TB
FE --> User: "Connected as {username}"

== Fetch Match History ==

FE -> API: syncMatchHistory()
activate API
API -> TB: invoke("sync_match_history")
activate TB

TB -> AC: get_match_history(steam_id)
activate AC
AC -> STEAM: GET /ICSGOServers_730/GetGameServersStatus
STEAM --> AC: Match list
AC --> TB: Matches[]
deactivate AC

loop for each match
    TB -> DB: Check if match exists
    alt New match
        TB -> DB: INSERT match
        TB -> TB: emit("new_match_found")
    end
end

TB --> API: SyncResult {new: 5, existing: 20}
deactivate TB
API --> FE: Update match list
deactivate API

FE --> User: "5 new matches found"

== Fetch Pro Player Data ==

User -> FE: Open "Compare with Pros"
activate FE

FE -> FE: Select player: "s1mple"
FE -> API: getProPlayerStats("s1mple")
activate API
API -> TB: invoke("get_pro_stats", {name: "s1mple"})
activate TB

TB -> DB: Check cache freshness
alt Cache valid (< 24h)
    DB --> TB: Cached stats
    TB --> API: ProStats (cached)
else Cache stale or missing
    TB -> AC: fetch_hltv_player("s1mple")
    activate AC
    
    AC -> HLTV: GET /player/7998/s1mple
    HLTV --> AC: Player page HTML
    AC -> AC: Parse HTML for stats
    AC --> TB: ProPlayerStats
    deactivate AC
    
    TB -> DB: UPDATE cache SET data = ..., fetched_at = NOW()
    TB --> API: ProStats (fresh)
end

deactivate TB
API --> FE: ProStats
deactivate API

FE -> FE: Display comparison

== Faceit Integration ==

User -> FE: Click "Connect Faceit"
FE -> API: initFaceitAuth()

note over FE, FACEIT: Similar OAuth flow as Steam

API -> TB: invoke("sync_faceit_matches")
activate TB

TB -> AC: get_faceit_matches(faceit_id)
activate AC
AC -> FACEIT: GET /players/{id}/history
FACEIT --> AC: Match history
AC --> TB: Matches[]
deactivate AC

TB -> TB: Correlate with existing demos\nby match_id or timestamp
TB -> DB: Update match records\nwith Faceit data (Elo, etc.)

TB --> API: FaceitSyncResult
deactivate TB

FE --> User: "Faceit data synced"

deactivate FE

== Rate Limiting ==

note over AC
  All API clients implement:
  - Request rate limiting
  - Exponential backoff
  - Request queuing
  - Cache-first strategy
end note

@enduml
